#
# This release reached these through WORKSPACE-era http_archive repos with LLVM's
# own BUILD files. The generated MODULE.bazel now declares the BCR modules
# upstream main uses (zlib-ng as @llvm_zlib, zstd as @llvm_zstd, mpfr, gmp,
# libpfm as @pfm), and this patch mirrors upstream's consumer side:
# //third-party:zlib and :zstd wrappers (9626c90c335c, ac4cf404d8f3) carry the
# LLVM_ENABLE_* defines, and the mpfr/pfm selects point at the BCR targets with
# local libmpfr_system/libpfm_system shims (ef86984f539f). Two redist additions:
# `pfm_external` is limited to Linux, since libpfm is Linux-only and the BCR
# module has no gate, and mpfr_impl inherits libc's Windows incompatibility.
